+Swear words are masked in captions and the hook by default (F*CK, Х*Й, P*RRA); `--no-censor` turns that off.
+With `translation.json` the log says `captions: translated to pt`: each translated line is on screen during
+the original phrase and its words light up spread over that span (not word-synced with the audio, since word
+order differs between languages). The sync check below still applies.
+
+**Speech x caption sync (mandatory).** For every clip the render measures the finished `.mp4`:
+1. `speech`: where the clip's audio lands in the original audio (which the transcript timed). Tolerance 40 ms;
+   outside it the clip is re-encoded automatically with the corrected cut.
+2. `captions`: when each word's yellow highlight changes on screen vs. when the word is spoken. Tolerance 120 ms.
+Result in the log (`sync: speech ok (+0 ms), captions ok (+0 ms)`), in `clip.json` and in `report.md`.
+`FAIL` in either = clip rejected: don't deliver it, investigate (cut, filter timestamps) and render again.
+`unclear` (little speech, loud music / game audio, no visible highlight) = check it yourself: extract a frame at
+a word's time (`words.json`) and see that the caption highlights that word.
+`speech skipped` is expected for a local file (nothing was cut out of a download, so there is nothing to drift);
+the overall status is then `check`: rely on the `captions` result.
+Manual fine-tuning, only when everything is ok and it still looks off: `--caption-lead` (positive = earlier,
+negative = later; use `=` with negatives, e.g. `--caption-lead=-0.1`).
+Render look (default, nothing to ask): 12% punch-in zoom on the loudest / fastest narration (`--zoom 1.2` stronger,
+`--no-zoom` off) and a brand overlay - thin purple neon frame + profile handle - read from `brand` in
+`~/.ai-stream-clipper/config.json` (`{"frame": true, "handle": "@profile"}`; `--no-brand` turns it off for one
+render). Every clip also gets a cover `<clip>_capa.jpg` (1080x1920: the strongest frame, color-graded, two other
+moments as neon-bordered cards, the hook in big letters and the brand; `--no-cover` turns it off).
+Only pass `--no-zoom` / `--no-brand` / `--no-cover` when the request says so. To change the handle or the frame (only
+when the user asks): `clipper.py brand --handle @profile` (`--handle ""` removes it, `--frame off` removes the frame).
 The facecam crop is face and shoulders: whole head, the streamer's whole movement range, and stream
 overlays (donation widgets, logos, chat) either fully out or fully in, never cut in half (magenta boxes
 in `layout_debug.jpg`). The hook is a big white plate at the top for the first 2.6 s, above the face.
 
